---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { SITE } from '../../site';
---
<BaseLayout title="Privacy & cookies" description="How this site uses cookies and Google Analytics, and how to change your choice.">
  <section class="page-header">
    <div class="container">
      <p class="eyebrow">Privacy</p>
      <h1>Privacy &amp; cookies</h1>
      <p class="lead">This site collects as little as possible. No ads, no cross-site tracking, no selling data.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="container" style="padding-bottom: 6rem;">
    <div class="prose">
      <h2>Who I am</h2>
      <p>
        This is the personal site of {SITE.name}, based in {SITE.location}. For any privacy question or request,
        email <a href={`mailto:${SITE.email}`}>{SITE.email}</a>.
      </p>

      <h2>Analytics (only with your consent)</h2>
      <p>
        If you click <strong>Accept</strong> on the cookie banner, the site loads Google Analytics 4 to count page
        views and see which articles get read. Google then collects the pages you visit, the referring site, your
        browser and device type, and your approximate location (country or city). Google Analytics 4 does not log or store IP
        addresses. Google Signals and ad personalisation are turned off.
      </p>
      <p>
        Google Ireland Ltd processes this data on my behalf and may transfer it to the US under the EU–US Data
        Privacy Framework and UK Extension. See <a href="https://policies.google.com/privacy">Google’s privacy
        policy</a>. Analytics data is kept for 14 months.
      </p>
      <p>
        The legal basis is your consent. If you click <strong>Reject</strong> or ignore the banner, Google Analytics is never
        loaded.
      </p>

      <h2>Cookies and local storage</h2>
      <table>
        <thead>
          <tr><th>Name</th><th>Purpose</th><th>Duration</th></tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr><td><code>_ga</code></td><td>Google Analytics: tells visits apart (only after consent)</td><td>2 years</td></tr>
          <tr><td><code>_ga_&lt;id&gt;</code></td><td>Google Analytics: keeps session state (only after consent)</td><td>2 years</td></tr>
          <tr><td><code>cookie-consent</code></td><td>Remembers your analytics choice (local storage)</td><td>Until cleared</td></tr>
          <tr><td><code>theme</code></td><td>Remembers light/dark mode (local storage)</td><td>Until cleared</td></tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>

      <h2>Changing your mind</h2>
      <p>
        Use <a href="#" data-cookie-settings>Cookie settings</a> (also in the footer) at any time. If you reject,
        the analytics cookies are deleted.
      </p>

      <h2>Your rights</h2>
      <p>
        Under UK GDPR you can ask to access or delete personal data, or complain to the
        <a href="https://ico.org.uk/make-a-complaint/">Information Commissioner’s Office</a>.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
